description:
Design a module that converts an 8-bit binary number into its equivalent Gray code representation. The first bit of the Gray code output is identical to the first bit of the binary input, and each subsequent bit is determined by performing a XOR operation between the current binary bit and the previous binary bit. This implementation ensures that only one bit changes at a time during transitions, which is the primary characteristic of Gray code.
module top_module(
  input [7:0] bin,
  output reg [7:0] gray  // Changed to reg type to allow assignment in always block
);

code:
module top_module(
  input [7:0] bin,
  output reg [7:0] gray  // Changed to reg type to allow assignment in always block
);reg [7:0] gray_temp;
  integer i;

  always @* begin
    gray_temp[0] = bin[0];
    for(i = 1; i < 8; i = i + 1) begin
      gray_temp[i] = bin[i] ^ gray_temp[i - 1];
    end
    gray = gray_temp;  // This assignment is now valid since gray is reg type
  end
endmodule

