Design a circuit that performs a complex multiplication operation on a 32-bit input. The module takes a 32-bit data input and processes it through a series of left shifts and arithmetic operations to derive a final 32-bit output. Specifically, the circuit multiplies the input by a factor that combines various shifts and additions, effectively performing a tailored multiplication algorithm while maintaining a manageable 32-bit output size.
