description:
Design a circuit to compute the absolute value of a 16-bit signed integer input. The module takes a 16-bit signed integer as input and produces a 16-bit output, which is the absolute value of the input. It uses a series of sequential stages to determine if the input is negative; if so, it negates the input to produce the absolute value; otherwise, it simply forwards the input.
module top_module(
    input signed [15:0] in,
    output reg [15:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
    input signed [15:0] in,
    output reg [15:0] out
);reg signed [15:0] stage1_out;
reg signed [15:0] stage2_out;

always @(in) begin
    stage1_out <= in;
end

always @(stage1_out) begin
    if (stage1_out < 0) begin
        stage2_out <= -stage1_out;
    end else begin
        stage2_out <= stage1_out;
    end
end

always @(stage2_out) begin
    out <= stage2_out;
end

endmodule

