description:
Design a circuit that reverses the order of an 8-bit input vector. The module takes an 8-bit input (`in_vec`) and produces an 8-bit output (`out_vec`), whereby the bits in the output are arranged such that the first bit of the input corresponds to the last bit of the output and so on. This effectively mirrors the input vector in a bitwise manner.
module top_module(
  input [7:0] in_vec,
  output reg [7:0] out_vec
);

code:
module top_module(
  input [7:0] in_vec,
  output reg [7:0] out_vec
);integer i;
reg temp;

always @(*) begin
  for(i=0; i<4; i=i+1) begin
    temp = in_vec[i];
    out_vec[i] = in_vec[7-i];
    out_vec[7-i] = temp;
  end
end

endmodule

