Implement a 4-to-2 encoded output circuit based on a 4-bit input. The module maps the input values into four distinct output cases: inputs 0 through 3 yield an output of 00; inputs 4 through 7 yield 01; inputs 8 through 11 yield 10; and any other inputs produce a default output of 11. This design effectively categorizes the input into four ranges and encodes them into a two-bit output.
